    {
        "user": "UGWUJUZHT",
        "type": "message",
        "ts": "1761994764.110879",
        "client_msg_id": "7559add4-92c8-4e04-a5b0-1f17ac41baf5",
        "text": "FWIW, aside: what I see in this is something that Jef Raskin discussed in \u201cThe Humane Interface\u201d. Measuring and increasing the size of the target area of buttons and selectable doo-dads. Now that I\u2019m retired, I am discovering a lot of horrible UI problems in everything I use. I\u2019ve had to disable cmd-Q in MacOS and ^X^C in emacs (due to increased finger-slop, I hit ^X and ^C together when I mean to hit only ^X). I regularly type cmd-C when I mean cmd-V only due to the physical closeness of those keys. I regularly click on the Claude icon in the dock when I mean to click on <http://draw.io|draw.io>, due to the similarity in background colour (orange) and the relative density of the foreground image (white splat for Claude vs. white node-and-wire for <http://draw.io|draw.io>, both filling about 75% of the icon, vs. the Pages icon which has an orange background but with only 30%-ish white foreground image). Disappearing and reappearing scroll bars and dock-bars are plain annoying. Auto-rearrangement of menu items (e.g. by recently used) is annoying and confusing - I first noticed this problem in SBCL\u2019s restart menu (ultra-horrible UI, due to inconsistency).",
        "team": "T5TCAFTA9",
        "thread_ts": "1761891896.324109",
        "parent_user_id": "UCUSW7WVD",
        "blocks": [
            {
                "type": "rich_text",
                "block_id": "pV6lr",
                "elements": [
                    {
                        "type": "rich_text_section",
                        "elements": [
                            {
                                "type": "text",
                                "text": "FWIW, aside: what I see in this is something that Jef Raskin discussed in \u201cThe Humane Interface\u201d. Measuring and increasing the size of the target area of buttons and selectable doo-dads. Now that I\u2019m retired, I am discovering a lot of horrible UI problems in everything I use. I\u2019ve had to disable cmd-Q in MacOS and ^X^C in emacs (due to increased finger-slop, I hit ^X and ^C together when I mean to hit only ^X). I regularly type cmd-C when I mean cmd-V only due to the physical closeness of those keys. I regularly click on the Claude icon in the dock when I mean to click on "
                            },
                            {
                                "type": "link",
                                "url": "http://draw.io",
                                "text": "draw.io"
                            },
                            {
                                "type": "text",
                                "text": ", due to the similarity in background colour (orange) and the relative density of the foreground image (white splat for Claude vs. white node-and-wire for "
                            },
                            {
                                "type": "link",
                                "url": "http://draw.io",
                                "text": "draw.io"
                            },
                            {
                                "type": "text",
                                "text": ", both filling about 75% of the icon, vs. the Pages icon which has an orange background but with only 30%-ish white foreground image). Disappearing and reappearing scroll bars and dock-bars are plain annoying. Auto-rearrangement of menu items (e.g. by recently used) is annoying and confusing - I first noticed this problem in SBCL\u2019s restart menu (ultra-horrible UI, due to inconsistency)."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ]
            }
        ],
